Dear Jennifer,

As I prepare for my retirement, I am officially handing over the inspection program for the ATU-100 to you. Please ensure you are familiar with QSCP-IP-ATU100 Rev 2, which governs the CUI program for insulated lines. Per this plan, profile RT or insulation windows must be executed every 5 years for lines operating within the CUI range.

Additionally, please review QSCP-DMR-2014-002 regarding the DEA strength increase. Due to the higher acid-gas loading and expected corrosion rates, the rich amine circuits are now on a 3-year thickness interval with additional CMLs located downstream of the let-down valve. As the new Inspection Coordinator, Jennifer Walsh will now be responsible for all future scheduling and NCR management for this unit.

Best regards, Douglas Ferreira

Douglas Ferreira, Inspection Supervisor, API 570 inspector, QSCP Hamilton Inspection Department